            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2 id="posts-en">Major Posts Under MPSC Gazetted Services</h2>
        <p>Based on the final merit list of the examination, direct appointments are made to the following Class 1 and Class 2 officer positions:</p>
        <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse my-6">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-primary/10">
              <th class="p-3 border border-border-card font-bold text-text-main">Category (Class)</th>
              <th class="p-3 border border-border-card font-bold text-text-main">Major Posts (Vacancy List)</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 border border-border-card font-semibold">Class A (Class 1)</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-border-card">Deputy Collector, Deputy Superintendent of Police / Assistant Commissioner of Police (DySP/ACP), Assistant Commissioner of State Tax, Chief Executive Officer / Block Development Officer (BDO - Class 1), Tehsildar, District Deputy Registrar.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 border border-border-card font-semibold">Class B (Class 2)</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-border-card">Naib Tehsildar, Block Development Officer (BDO - Class 2), Assistant Registrar (Cooperative Societies), Section Officer (Mantralaya), Deputy Superintendent (Land Records).</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <h2 id="eligibility-en">Eligibility Criteria and Age Limits</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Educational Qualification:</strong> Candidates must hold a graduation degree in any discipline from a recognized university. Final-year students are also eligible to appear for the preliminary examination.</li>
          <li><strong>Age Limit (General/Open Category):</strong> Minimum age is 19 years and maximum age is 38 years. Reserved category candidates get a relaxation of 5 years (up to 43 years).</li>
          <li><strong>Physical Requirements (Specifically for DySP Post):</strong> For male candidates, a minimum height of 165 cm and a chest of 84 cm without expansion (with a minimum of 5 cm expansion required) is mandatory. For female candidates, the minimum height required is 157 cm.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="exam-pattern-en">Revised Exam Pattern and Selection Stages</h2>
        <p>The MPSC Gazetted Civil Services examination is conducted in three successive stages:</p>
        <div class="space-y-4 pl-2 border-l-2 border-primary/30 my-6">
          <div>
            <h4 class="text-text-main font-bold m-0">1. Preliminary Exam - 400 Marks (Objective MCQs)</h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-muted m-0">Consists of two papers of 200 marks each: General Studies (GS Paper 1) and Civil Services Aptitude Test (CSAT Paper 2). CSAT is qualifying in nature, requiring a minimum score of 33% (66 marks) to clear.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="text-text-main font-bold m-0">2. Mains Exam - 1750 Marks (Written Descriptive)</h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-muted m-0">Based on the new UPSC-aligned descriptive pattern, it includes 9 papers in total. There are 7 merit-ranking papers (GS 1, GS 2, GS 3, GS 4, Essay, and two optional subject papers) and 2 language qualifying papers.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="text-text-main font-bold m-0">3. Interview / Personality Test - 275 Marks</h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-muted m-0">Candidates clearing the descriptive Mains are invited for a personality test conducted by the Commission panel to evaluate administrative aptitude and overall suitability.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

