        <div class="space-y-4 mt-3 mb-8">
          <div class="bg-bg-surface border border-border-card p-5 rounded-2xl">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-text-main mb-2">FAQ 1: Is the CSAT paper in MPSC Gazetted Prelims qualifying in nature?</h3>
            <p class="text-text-muted m-0">Answer 1: Yes, the Civil Services Aptitude Test (CSAT) is purely qualifying. Candidates must score a minimum of 33% (66 out of 200 marks) in it. The final merit list for Mains qualification is determined solely by the marks obtained in General Studies (GS Paper 1).</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-bg-surface border border-border-card p-5 rounded-2xl">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-text-main mb-2">FAQ 2: How does the new Optional Subject system work in the Mains exam?</h3>
            <p class="text-text-muted m-0">Answer 2: In the revised descriptive pattern, candidates have to select one optional subject from a list of 26 subjects provided by the MPSC. The optional subject consists of two descriptive papers, totaling 500 marks.</p>
